# S3 (audit_builtins): exit()'s ungranted refusal surface — a differential
# golden. rust (sec-r2, audit C-11): process exit is a capability,
# default-deny; the refusal is a catchable interference stress and the
# runner SURVIVES. The oracle's old unconditional sys.exit() diverged here
# (process died, rc mismatch) — the faithful mirror now refuses the same
# way. The GRANTED exit (rc = N, the ok side) is Rust-runner-only surface
# under --allow-exit / .cell allow.exit = true: a real process exit cannot
# be a byte-comparison target in the sequential lane, the refusal is.
print("reached")
stress {
    exit(3)
} rescue (e) {
    print("[" + e.kind + "] " + e.message)
}
print("runner survived the refusal")
